# Read by BuildKit for packages/site/Dockerfile, whose context is the repo root -
# a Dockerfile-specific ignore file, so the repo root needs no .dockerignore.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/out
build
.git
.github
.cache
.idea
**/.DS_Store
# Secrets must never reach a build context. `**/` because ignore patterns are
# anchored at the context root, and Dokploy writes its .env next to the
# Dockerfile, in packages/site/ - where Next's standalone output would also
# copy it into the image.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/*.pem
packages/site/public/demo
